Page1: ADMINISTRATIVE ORDER 2024-08 SECOND AMENDMENT
IN RE: ACTIVE, DIFFERENTIAL CIVIL CASE MANAGEMENT
I. All County and Circuit Court Civil Cases
Each judge assigned to any civil case is hereby directed to actively manage each civil case and to enter an initial Case Management Order as described below.
Footnote1: This Order does not apply to small claims cases, except as provided in Rule 1.200(a)(3).
Page2 sectionIV: For each civil case, the Plaintiff shall serve an initial Case Management Order with the complaint and summons on each defendant.
Page3 sectionVI: The Clerk must issue a Case Management Order in all new cases at the time the case is created.
Page3 sectionIX: This amendment is effective immediately and shall rescind all prior versions.
Page3 signature date: 1 day of October 2025.
